;==============================================================================
;                     ■ 拡張子別実行の書式について ■
;
; .1
;	<.???> TAB or SPACE <command[option]> TAB or SPACE [rem]
;	   ^                        ^                        ^
;	   |                        |                        + ｺﾒﾝﾄの入力
;	   |                        |
;	   |                        + 実行させたいｺﾏﾝﾄﾞの入力 (ﾏｸﾛの使用が可能)
;          |
;          + 反応させたい拡張子の入力
;
; .2
;	<:command> TAB or SPACE <command[option]> TAB or SPACE [rem]
;	    ^                       ^                            ^
;	    |                       |                            + ｺﾒﾝﾄの入力
;	    |                       |
;	    |                       + 実行させたいｺﾏﾝﾄﾞの入力 (ﾏｸﾛの使用が可能)
;           |
;           + 反応させたいﾌｧｲﾙﾈｰﾑの入力
;
;==============================================================================


; The following options can be used when executing an external program:
;
;	$A =	Drive input on commandline
;	$F =    Filename input on commandline
;	$C =	Filename of current file
;	$X =	Filename of current file (without extension)
;	$D =	Current drive
;	$d =	Temporary drive (that is in environment item TEMP)
;	$J =	Execute program in Kanji-mode
;	$K =	Ask for any key before returning to Multi Mente
;	$k =	Ask for any key after each command (inserts PAUSE)
;	$P =	Current path
;	$R =	Put a RETURN in the commandline
;	$T =	Filenames of selected files (one by one)
;	$t =	Same as $T, but without extension
;	$M =	Filenames of selected files (all behind eachother)
;	$m =	Same as $M, but without extension
;	$V =	Show file with internal viewer
;	$$ =	Put a "$" in the commandline 
;	$Z =	Uncrunch file, dependant of file-extension
;
;-------------------------------------------------------------

;==============================================================================
;  MSX SD Maker: what RETURN does with each file type on this card
;==============================================================================
; How MM 2.07 reads this file (checked in MM.COM and in openMSX):
;  - Only lines that start in column 0 with '.' (extension) or ':' (full
;    name, e.g. :AUTOEXEC.BAT) count; anything else is a comment. Patterns
;    in UPPERCASE; '?' matches any character. The FIRST matching line wins,
;    so full names go first and '.???' last (nothing after it is ever used).
;  - A TAB between pattern and command, and before a comment: text after a
;    SPACE goes to the program. A pattern with no command runs the next line.
;  - MM reads only the first 16383 bytes and re-reads the file on every
;    RETURN: just save it. %VARIABLES% (%MM%...) are expanded when it runs.
;  - $T runs the command once per tagged file; $M puts them all in one line
;    (about 100 characters, the rest goes to a second command). With nothing
;    tagged both take the file under the cursor. With files tagged, RETURN
;    uses the line of the file UNDER THE CURSOR and gives it the TAGGED
;    files: move the cursor onto one of them first (SPACE moves it down).
;  - MM expands $T/$M in the buffer that holds this file: a $T/$M line must
;    be further from the start than (tagged files x expanded line) bytes.
;    That is why these notes go first and the $T/$M lines last.
;  - While a $T list runs it stays in memory under MSX-DOS: about 11 tagged
;    files take 256 bytes of TPA, and VGMPLAY needs about 53 KB of it: about
;    30 songs per RETURN fit, about 10 with MGSDRV resident (more give
;    "Insufficient TPA space"; measured in openMSX, Nextor 2.1.4, 7 drives).
;  - MSX SD Maker leaves out the lines whose program is not on the card;
;    those files open in the viewer ('.???').
;
; What the lines need:
;  .ROM .DSK .ZIP  SofaRun: SROM picks the ROM device by itself, SRI boots the
;  .MIG .SG        disk (write-protected: W in SRI changes it), SUZ lists the
;                  ZIP ([U] extracts it here), MIGVIEW, SSMS (SG-1000).
;  .VGM .VGZ       VGMPLAY: the 1.4 of MUSICA, first in the PATH (without
;                  MUSICA, the 1.2 of SofaRun). Tagged songs play in turn;
;                  CTRL+STOP stops the list.
;  .MFM .MWM       ROBOPLAY (MUSICA\ROBOPLAY, in the PATH: it loads its .PLY
;                  from its own folder): OPL4, MoonBlaster FM and Wave songs,
;                  USER and EDIT mode. It loads the wavekit named in the song
;                  (else SONG.MWK) from the song's folder; with none an FM
;                  song uses the ROM tones. ESC ends a song, CTRL+STOP between
;                  two ends the list. RoboPlay uses 0xC000-0xD3FF: about 30
;                  tagged songs per RETURN; with more it goes back to DOS.
;  .MWK            MWMPLAY (MUSICA): a USER song with a wavekit of another
;                  name: tag both, cursor on the .MWK, RETURN.
;  .MOD            MMP: OPL4 with sample RAM.     .PT3  PT3PLAY: PSG.
;  .MBM .MBK       MBMPLAY: MSX-MUSIC / MSX-AUDIO. .MCM MCDRV: MSX-MUSIC.
;  .MUS            MGSC + MGSDRV (the AUTOEXEC sets MGSDRV to its path).
;  .MID            MIDIPLAY: only with a MIDI-PAC.
;  .PCM .CRT       PCMPLAY (turbo R PCM, else PSG), CHRIS (turbo R PCM
;                  only: it hangs on a machine without it).
;  .TMU            TriloTracker (SCC); it starts empty.
;  .EMU            EMUFILE (Nextor): resets into the disk image set.
;  .UPD            MXUPDATE: checks the file and asks before flashing.
;  .MGS            MM plays it by itself once MGSDRV is resident: SHIFT+RETURN
;                  installs it and comes back to MM (pressed again, it removes
;                  MGSDRV).
;==============================================================================

:AUTOEXEC.BAT	$V	run from MM it would get no %1 and break the PATH
:XSYS.BAT	$V	swaps MSXDOS2.SYS and NEXTOR.SYS and resets
:SETALIAS.BAT	$V	aliases of another machine
:MBFM.CFG	$V	binary settings of MoonBlaster FM
:MBWAVE.CFG	$V	binary settings of MoonBlaster Wave
:EMUDSK.ROM	$V	disk emulator ROM for RUNIT, not a game
.ARC	UNARC $C$K	list
.ARJ	UNARJ L $C$K	list
.ARK	UNARC $C$K	list
.ASC	BASIC $C
.BAS	BASIC $C
.BAT	$C
.CFG	AKID $C
.COM	$C$K
.CRT	CHRIS $C
.DSK	SRI $C$K
.EMU	EMUFILE SET $C$K
.GIF	DAGIF $C
.INI	AKID $C
.LZH	PMEXT $C$K	list
.MBK	MBMPLAY $C
.MCM	MCDRV $C
.MID	MIDIPLAY $C$K	;MIDRY $C /I31	;SMF $C
.MUS	MGSC $C -P -N$K
.PMA	PMEXT $C$K	list
.ROM	SROM $C$K
.SG	SSMS $C$K
.TMU	TT $C
.TXT	AKID $C
.UPD	MXUPDATE $C$K
.ZIP	SUZ L $C$K	list
.BMP	BMP $T
.GE5	BLS $T /S5
.GRA	BLS $T
.JPG	JPD $T
.MAG	BLS $T
.MAX	BLS $T
.MIG	MIGVIEW $T
.MKI	BLS $T
.MOD	MMP $T
.MSA	MSA $T
.MWK	MWMPLAY $M$K
.PCM	PCMPLAY $T
.PI	PI $T
.PIC	BLS $T
.PT3	PT3PLAY $T
.SC5	BLS $T
.SC6	BLS $T
.SC7	BLS $T
.SC8	BLS $T
.SCA	BLS $T
.SCB	BLS $T
.SCC	BLS $T
.SR5	BLS $T
.SR6	BLS $T
.SR7	BLS $T
.SR8	BLS $T
.SRA	BLS $T
.SRB	BLS $T
.VGM	VGMPLAY $T
.VGZ	VGMPLAY $T
.MBM	MBMPLAY $T -D
.MFM	ROBOPLAY $T
.MWM	ROBOPLAY $T
.???	$V	must stay the last line

